# MEWP telematics tracker — custom design rules
# Milestone 4. Written 2026-09-04.
#
# Netclass clearances live in telematics-tracker.kicad_pro. These rules cover
# the things a netclass clearance cannot express, chiefly the HV-to-signal
# separation, which is directional: HV must stand off low-voltage signals, but
# an HV part's own ground return (TVS, bulk caps) is necessarily close to its
# HV pad and must not be flagged.

(version 1)

# --- HV zone -------------------------------------------------------------
# handoff section 7: "HV zone (VIN up to 100 V) physically separated;
# >= 1.5 mm clearance HV-to-LV, marked keepout."
# GND is excepted by design: D2 SMDJ100A, C70/C71/C72/C73/C74 and R80 all
# return to GND right beside their HV pads. The electrical minimum still
# applies there via the HV netclass clearance (0.6 mm, IPC-2221 Table 6-1
# external uncoated at 100 V).
# Scoped to the HV_ZONE rule area on purpose. This is a board-level zone
# separation requirement, not an intra-package one: U5's exposed pad is VIN_B
# at up to 100 V and the EG11752 package puts its own signal pins 0.55 mm from
# it, so an unscoped rule is unsatisfiable and would mask real violations
# everywhere else. The universal electrical minimum is the HV netclass
# clearance (0.60 mm, IPC-2221 table 6-1 external uncoated at 100 V), which
# does apply everywhere. See design-log F-20.
(rule "HV to signal 1.5mm"
	(constraint clearance (min 1.5mm))
	(condition "A.insideArea('HV_ZONE') && A.NetClass == 'HV' && B.NetClass != 'HV' && B.NetClass != 'GND'"))

# Board-edge standoff for HV nets: creepage to a cut edge, and to whatever the
# housing presents beyond it.
(rule "HV to board edge"
	(constraint edge_clearance (min 1.0mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'HV'"))

# --- RF ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 50 ohm CPWG on L1 over the L2 GND plane, JLC7628 h = 0.2104 mm:
# W = 0.40 mm, G = 0.30 mm (48.9-50.4 ohm across Dk 4.3-4.6).
# The gap is held by the RF netclass clearance; this pins the width so a
# stray narrower segment cannot pass DRC unnoticed.
(rule "RF trace width"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.4mm) (opt 0.4mm) (max 0.4mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'RF'"))

# --- JLCPCB process floor ------------------------------------------------
# Skill file section PCB: 0.15 mm track/space is the safe figure for the
# standard 4-layer process.
(rule "JLCPCB min track"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.Type == 'track'"))

(rule "JLCPCB min via"
	(constraint hole_size (min 0.3mm))
	(constraint via_diameter (min 0.45mm))
	(condition "A.Type == 'via'"))

(rule "JLCPCB hole to hole"
	(constraint hole_to_hole (min 0.5mm)))

# --- thermal / current ---------------------------------------------------
# handoff section 4: VBAT_MODEM carries the modem's 2 A transmit burst and is
# specified >= 2 mm wide. Enforced so a narrow neck cannot slip through.
# The 2.0 mm trunk requirement lives in the MODEM_BULK netclass track width,
# which is what the router uses. This floor is deliberately lower: the trace
# has to neck down to enter U1's pad row, which is on a 1.30 mm pitch - a 2 mm
# trace landing there bridges the neighbouring pads. A hard 2 mm minimum makes
# the only physically possible entry illegal.
(rule "VBAT_MODEM minimum width"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'MODEM_BULK' && A.Type == 'track'"))

# --- F-20: the buck's exposed pad is at line voltage ---------------------
# EG11752 pin 9 (the SOIC-8 exposed pad) is VIN_B, i.e. up to 100 V, and the
# package places its own signal pins 0.55 mm from it (EP 3.30 x 2.40 centred,
# signal pads at y = +/-2.72 with 1.94 mm height -> inner edge +/-1.75 against
# an EP edge at +/-1.20). No layout can widen that: it is the package.
#
# 0.60 mm is the IPC-2221 table 6-1 figure for EXTERNAL UNCOATED conductors at
# 100 V; coated (B4) at 100 V is about 0.25 mm, so 0.55 mm passes with better
# than 2:1 margin ONCE COATED.
#
# CONFIRMED 2026-09-05: conformal coating is MANDATORY on every board including
# prototypes, and is logged as a safety-critical process requirement (handoff
# section 6.1, SKILL.md P1). Prototypes are coated before the 100 V / 85 C
# burn-in, and the U5 area carries a coating inspection marking on F.Fab.
#
# THIS EXCEPTION IS VALID ONLY WHILE THAT REQUIREMENT HOLDS. If coating is ever
# dropped, this rule must be deleted and U5 reconsidered - an uncoated board
# relies on the package's own certified spacing alone and must not be
# energised at line voltage.
(rule "U5 package internal HV spacing"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.3mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('U5') && B.insideCourtyard('U5')"))

# --- CHECK 3: intra-component HV->LV exemption at <= 40 V -----------------
# Agreed policy: a pad pair INSIDE one component is exempt from the 1.5 mm
# zone-separation rule where the voltage across that part is <= 40 V, because
# the part IS the HV->LV transition and its pad spacing is the package.
# The sense dividers are 3 x 100k then 9.1k = 309.1 kohm, so at VIN = 100 V the
# current is 323.5 uA and each 100k drops 32.35 V - inside the exemption.
(rule "divider internal spacing <=40V"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('R30') && B.insideCourtyard('R30')"))
(rule "divider internal spacing <=40V R31"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('R31') && B.insideCourtyard('R31')"))
(rule "divider internal spacing <=40V R32"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('R32') && B.insideCourtyard('R32')"))
(rule "divider internal spacing <=40V R33"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('R33') && B.insideCourtyard('R33')"))
(rule "divider internal spacing <=40V R34"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('R34') && B.insideCourtyard('R34')"))
(rule "divider internal spacing <=40V R35"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.5mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('R35') && B.insideCourtyard('R35')"))

# Above 40 V and therefore NOT covered by that exemption. These rest on the
# IPC-2221 figure for their actual voltage (0.60 mm uncoated at <= 100 V) plus
# the mandatory conformal coating - the same basis as F-20 at U5. Q1/Q2 are the
# DO FETs (LV gate, HV drain, SOT-23 pitch); R40 is the DNP spare divider and
# is a SINGLE 100k, so it sees 91.7 V where the fitted dividers see 32.35 V.
(rule "DO FET package spacing Q1"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.6mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('Q1') && B.insideCourtyard('Q1')"))
(rule "DO FET package spacing Q2"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.6mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('Q2') && B.insideCourtyard('Q2')"))
(rule "spare divider R40 package spacing"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.6mm))
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('R40') && B.insideCourtyard('R40')"))

# X1 vendor footprint: 0.19 mm between its own GND and card-detect pads. Fixed
# by the part, documented waiver.
(rule "X1 vendor footprint internal spacing"
	(constraint clearance (min 0.15mm))
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('X1') && B.memberOfFootprint('X1')"))

